<title>USA: Mass Turnpike might eliminate more western tolls.</title>
<headline>Mass Turnpike might eliminate more western tolls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts Turnpike Authority officials said they are considering eliminating westbound tolls at the Allston, Brighton, and at the Route-128 toll booths.</p>
<p>However, travellers headed for Boston would see their tolls doubled to $1. The Turnpike Authority presented the plan as a way to ease traffic in the area.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
